meta {
  name: Reopen Run
  type: http
  seq: 39
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/carrier-reconciliation/runs/{{reconRunId}}/reopen
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{reconToken}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 201", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(201);
  });

  test("the run is open again", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.id).to.equal(bru.getVar("reconRunId"));
    expect(body.closedAt).to.equal(null);
    expect(body.closedBy).to.equal(null);
  });
}

docs {
  # POST /carrier-reconciliation/runs/:id/reopen — reopen a closed month

  - **Module:** `carrier_reconciliation`
  - **Permission:** `carrier_reconciliation:write`

  The month's open rows are back on their assignees' lists, and its rows can
  be handed to people again.

  Except a row whose assignee can no longer be given rows — they left the
  agency, or lost `leads:write`, while the month was closed. A work transfer
  or release never saw that row (it was on no list), so it starts with nobody
  on it, as a re-upload treats a carried assignment. A decided row keeps
  whoever worked it.

  Idempotent: reopening an open month answers the run unchanged. Runs last in
  the folder, so a re-run starts from an open month.

  ## Response `201`

  The run (`ReconciliationRunDetail`), `closedAt` and `closedBy` both `null`.

  ## Errors
  - `400` — `:id` is not an ObjectId
  - `403` — no `carrier_reconciliation:write`
  - `404` — no such run in the agency
  - `409` — a re-upload replaced the run, or the run did not finish
}
